[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3089141756","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108725#issuecomment-3089141756","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108725","id":3089141756,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc64II_8","user":{"login":"Bromeon","id":708488,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwODQ4OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/708488?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon","html_url":"https://github.com/Bromeon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-18T11:21:17Z","updated_at":"2025-07-18T11:21:17Z","body":"> I'd go as far to say as we should consider squeezing this into 4.5. As a new interface, it should be impossible for this to introduce new bugs, and it would be nice to already use it with godot-cpp in the 4.5 release (rather than in half a year from now).\r\n\r\nThe risk is more that an API is stabilized that then has to be indefinitely supported, whereas adding it after would give the whole 4.6 cycle for review, testing and feedback. At least this was the reasoning for the `RequiredPtr` change, even though one part (the `meta` information) could have been added in a purely backwards-compatible way.\r\n\r\nBut yes, lately there are only 2 Godot releases per year, which isn't great for GDExtension which is tied to minor releases. It comes down to a lot of these make-or-break scenarios :confused: ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3089141756/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3089275231","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108725#issuecomment-3089275231","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108725","id":3089275231,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc64Iplf","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-18T12:08:53Z","updated_at":"2025-07-18T12:08:53Z","body":"@Ivorforce:\r\n\r\n> I'd go as far to say as we should consider squeezing this into 4.5. As a new interface, it should be impossible for this to introduce new bugs, and it would be nice to already use it with godot-cpp in the 4.5 release (rather than in half a year from now).\r\n\r\nIf everyone was on board with this (including the production folks), I think it could be OK for 4.5. It mirrors what Godot has already had internally for a long time, so there isn't too much we could get wrong about this API.\r\n\r\nLet's chat about it at next week's GDExtension team meeting\r\n\r\n@Bromeon:\r\n\r\n> The risk is more that an API is stabilized that then has to be indefinitely supported, whereas adding it after would give the whole 4.6 cycle for review, testing and feedback.\r\n\r\nYeah, I agree. I only starting digging into this problem on Monday, so this would be a very quick turn around for making a core change to the GDExtension interface. Especially given that the problem has existed since Godot 4.0 was released, so it isn't a 4.5 release blocker or anything\r\n\r\nHowever, like I said above, as far as APIs go, this one does seem pretty safe given that mirrors a fairly stable internal API (even Godot 3.0 has the `p_pad_align` argument [on these functions](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/3.0/core/os/memory.h#L56))","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3089275231/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3104989761","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108725#issuecomment-3104989761","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108725","id":3104989761,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc65EmJB","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-22T22:18:28Z","updated_at":"2025-07-22T22:18:28Z","body":"Discussed at the GDExtension meeting, and we're OK with waiting for Godot 4.6 on this one. The issue has existed since Godot 4.0 and doesn't come up as often as other support issues. And this will allow us time to really test that debug and release builds can mixed and there are no other issues","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3104989761/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3354131645","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108725#issuecomment-3354131645","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108725","id":3354131645,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7H6_y9","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starr